title: The Assembly Reconvenes
subtitle: A new President of the Assembly must be elected.
view-if: chancellor == "Goodryke" and (next_reichstag_time == rubicon_time and next_reichstag_time > 0)
on-arrival: reichstag_pres_rubicon = 1
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/reichstag.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}
go-to: nsdap_lead if largest_party == "Royalist"; spd_lead if largest_party != "Royalist"

= Assembly Reconvenes

@nsdap_lead

The Assembly has reconvened for the first time since the election, with a significantly larger contingent of <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> members now present. The immediate issue at hand is the election of the President of the Assembly. While the position has traditionally been a procedural one, it has taken on heightened importance under Goodryke's presidential government, given the President's authority to influence the agenda and adjourn sessions.

By long-standing custom, the role is granted to the largest parliamentary delegation. That delegation is now the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>. The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> holds the balance of power. Will they uphold tradition and hand a key parliamentary post to an openly anti-constitutional party?

- @reichstag_calculations

@spd_lead

The Assembly has reconvened for the first time since the election, with a significantly larger contingent of <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> members now present. The immediate issue at hand is the election of the President of the Assembly. While the position has traditionally been a procedural one, it has taken on heightened importance under Goodryke's presidential government, given the President's authority to influence the agenda and adjourn sessions.

By long-standing custom, the role is granted to the largest parliamentary delegation. That delegation isn't the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, but the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> backing them nonetheless is a key part of negotiations between the two parties. Without such backing, it is likely that our candidate, Paul Löbe, would be elected once again.

- @reichstag_calculations

@reichstag_calculations
title: The votes are tallied...
go-to: goring if largest_party == "Royalist" and unionist_relation < 55 and gallax_right_coalition >= 50; spd if largest_party != "Royalist" or unionist_relation >= 55 or gallax_right_coalition < 50


@goring
on-arrival: {!
Q.next_reichstag_time = Q.rubicon_time + 2;
Q.next_reichstag_week = Q.week + 2;
Q.next_reichstag_month = Q.month;
Q.next_reichstag_year = Q.year;

if (Q.next_reichstag_week > 4) {
  Q.next_reichstag_week -= 4;
  Q.next_reichstag_month += 1;
}

if (Q.next_reichstag_week > 4) {
  Q.next_reichstag_week -= 4;
  Q.next_reichstag_month += 1;
}

if (Q.next_reichstag_month > 12) {
  Q.next_reichstag_month -= 12;
  Q.next_reichstag_year += 1;
}

Q.pro_republic -= 3;
Q.reichstag_goring = 1;
Q.reichstag_president = "Gorrick";
!}

With negotiations between the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> underway, previously hostile relations have thawed enough for the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> to support Hermann Gorrick’s election as President of the Assembly. The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> delegation’s newfound decorum convinced many that the party had turned over a new leaf.

In line with a promise made to the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>, the Assembly has adjourned for two more weeks to allow coalition talks to take place. Yet unease is growing within the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> at the possibility of a [+ royalist_chancellor +] chancellorship, and they may soon walk away from the table.

@spd
on-arrival: {!
Q.next_reichstag_time = Q.rubicon_time + 2;
Q.next_reichstag_week = Q.week + 2;
Q.next_reichstag_month = Q.month;
Q.next_reichstag_year = Q.year;

if (Q.next_reichstag_week > 4) {
  Q.next_reichstag_week -= 4;
  Q.next_reichstag_month += 1;
}

if (Q.next_reichstag_week > 4) {
  Q.next_reichstag_week -= 4;
  Q.next_reichstag_month += 1;
}

if (Q.next_reichstag_month > 12) {
  Q.next_reichstag_month -= 12;
  Q.next_reichstag_year += 1;
}

Q.pro_republic += 3;
Q.reichstag_goring = 0;
Q.reichstag_president = "Löbe";
if (!(Q.largest_party != "Royalist" && ((Q.weimar_coalition >= 40) || (Q.popular_front_coalition >= 50 && Q.collectivist_relation >= 50)))) Q.reichstag_president = "Eßer";
!}

[? if largest_party != "Royalist": In Assembly tradition, as the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> is the largest party, the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> feels bound to support us, regardless of our relations. ?][? if (unionist_relation >= 55 or gallax_right_coalition < 50) and largest_party == "Royalist": However, the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> simply cannot bring itself to support elevating a <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> to the Assembly presidency, breaking with tradition to elect our candidate. ?]

[? if largest_party != "Royalist" and ((weimar_coalition >= 40) or (popular_front_coalition >= 50 and collectivist_relation >= 50)): Paul Löbe is elected President of the Assembly once more, a position he held for the majority of the republic. ?][? if not (largest_party != "Royalist" and ((weimar_coalition >= 40) or (popular_front_coalition >= 50 and collectivist_relation >= 50))): Unfortunately, very few other parties are willing—or have the votes—to back our candidate, Paul Löbe, and the chamber instead settles on the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>'s Thomas Eßer. ?]

However, the Assembly agenda committee, over our objections, has voted for a two-week adjournment with the support of the parties to our right.